## Commercial Use Clarification

This section clarifies the commercial usage restrictions of the Licensed Work under the Business Source License 1.1.

The Licensed Work may not be used, in whole or in part, to create, offer, or distribute a commercial product or service where the Licensed Work itself constitutes a core functionality or primary component of the offering.

This includes, but is not limited to, hosting the Licensed Work as a service, providing it as a managed or SaaS offering, or integrating it into a commercial solution in a way that the resulting product relies on or competes with the Licensed Work.

It is permitted to provide paid professional services related to the Licensed Work, including installation, deployment, configuration, integration, maintenance, debugging, support, and consulting, provided that the Licensed Work is used by the client for internal purposes only and is not commercialized as part of a product or service offering.

For clarity, this License permits commercial activity around the Licensed Work (services), but not the commercialization of the Licensed Work itself or any derivative product where it becomes the primary value component.

This section is intended to further clarify the restrictions already defined under the Business Source License 1.1, and does not expand or replace the original license terms.

